  "limitations": [
    "One fresh direct Telnet process executes one edit or separately observed Q and R after the shrunk baseline and preparation are observed and acknowledged.",
    "Five or six stages preserve all three pre-edit observations; only phase 1 and the final phase resize.",
    "Explicit CUP positioning is a separate action and never substitutes for the natural post-resize cursor baseline.",
    "Document markers, protocol DSR and visible rectangles remain different observations; no internal storage or addressing policy is inferred.",
    "Preparation must retain the known tail, with only the declared L prefix for erase cases; unexpected preparation content is retained as a failure before edit acknowledgment.",
    "The finite allowlist admits bounded source-interval erasure with trailing spaces, one-cell insertion/deletion and declared edge writes; it is not an internal-policy prediction.",
    "Only 91x20 -> 61x20 -> 91x20 is covered, with no full grid, local-shell transport, reliability repetition or performance acceptance.",
